    <section class="pov-section">
      <div class="pov-eyebrow">WHAT WE'VE LEARNED</div>
      <h2>TikTok Shop is a human business.</h2>
      <div class="pov-signals">
        <article class="pov-signal">
          <h3>Creator access is infrastructure.</h3>
          <p>For a cold start, deep creator relationships matter. TikTok Shop isn't a capability you simply add to an ecommerce services menu.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pov-signal">
          <h3>The wrong partner costs more than their fee.</h3>
          <p>Lost time, wasted samples and six months of competitor momentum can be much harder to recover than the money you spent.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pov-signal">
          <h3>Sampling isn't a strategy.</h3>
          <p>Blindly sending free product and waiting for affiliate sales misses the point. Creator incentives, paid partnerships, content and commerce need to work together.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pov-signal">
          <h3>Channel GMV isn't the whole return.</h3>
          <p>TikTok Shop can create demand that converts elsewhere. Retail and DTC halo matter, so breaking even on the channel can still create meaningful enterprise value.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
